🚀 FULL SETUP COMMANDS (COPY–PASTE READY)
1. Update Ubuntu

sudo apt update

2. Install Python tools

sudo apt install python3 python3-pip python3-venv -y

3. Create project folder (optional but clean)

mkdir groq-ai
cd groq-ai

4. Create virtual environment

python3 -m venv groq-env

5. Activate environment

source groq-env/bin/activate

👉 You should now see:

(groq-env)

6. Install OpenAI SDK (used for Groq too)

pip install openai

7. Set Groq API key

export GROQ_API_KEY=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

(optional permanent)

echo 'export GROQ_API_KEY=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' >> ~/.bashrc
source ~/.bashrc

8. Create Python file

nano groq_test.py

9. Paste this code (IMPORTANT FIXED MODEL)

from openai import OpenAI
import os

client = OpenAI(
    api_key=os.getenv("GROQ_API_KEY"),
    base_url="https://api.groq.com/openai/v1"
)

response = client.chat.completions.create(
    model="llama-3.1-8b-instant",
    messages=[
        {"role": "user", "content": "Hello from Ubuntu using Groq AI!"}
    ]
)

print(response.choices[0].message.content)

10. Save file in nano

Press:

    CTRL + X
    Y
    Enter 

11. Run program

python groq_test.py
